; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Sunflower Seeds
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     phyllotaxis, golden angle, spirals, dot, square root
; SUMMARY:  Places seeds one by one, each turned by the golden angle, and the spirals of a sunflower head appear.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A sunflower grows its seeds from the middle. Each new seed is
;   turned about 137.5 degrees from the last one (the "golden
;   angle") and pushed out a little. The seeds pack together with no
;   gaps, and your eye sees spirals curving both ways. Two small
;   heads on the right use angles only slightly different, and the
;   neat packing falls apart into straight spokes.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the angles in the last lines and compare.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the golden angle: 360 x (1 - 1 / 1.618...) = 137.5 degrees
;   * placing seed n at distance c x sqrt(n) keeps the seeds evenly
;     spread, because the area of a circle grows like r x r
;   * DOT with a thick pen for round seeds
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Count the spirals going clockwise and anticlockwise. You will
;     find Fibonacci numbers like 21, 34 and 55.
;   * Try 137.3 and 137.7. How sensitive is the pattern?
;   * Use 90 degrees or 120 degrees. What do the seeds do?
; ============================================================

make "golden 360 * (1 - 1 / ((1 + sqrt 5) / 2))

; :count seeds round (cx, cy), :spread steps apart, turned :angle each.
to seedhead :cx :cy :count :spread :angle :seedsize
  for [n 1 :count] [
    localmake "r :spread * sqrt :n
    localmake "a :n * :angle
    ; inner seeds dark brown, outer seeds lighter and more golden
    localmake "t :n / :count
    setpencolor (list 90 + 120 * :t 50 + 90 * :t 20 + 10 * :t)
    setpensize :seedsize * (0.6 + 0.6 * :t)
    dot list :cx + :r * sin :a :cy + :r * cos :a
  ]
end

to petals :cx :cy :r :count
  setpencolor [250 200 40] setpensize 22
  repeat :count [
    penup setxy :cx :cy setheading 360 * repcount / :count + 5
    forward :r pendown forward 45
  ]
end

to caption :x :y :text
  penup setxy :x :y setpencolor [70 90 60] label :text
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [180 215 245]
setlabelheight 15
; the big flower: petals first, seeds on top
petals -120 10 212 34
seedhead -120 10 620 8.6 :golden 13
caption -230 -290 [137.5 degrees: the golden angle]
; two small heads with angles that are slightly wrong
seedhead 275 150 230 7 137 10
caption 230 20 [137 degrees]
seedhead 275 -130 230 7 140 10
caption 230 -260 [140 degrees]
